## 4. Platform Comparison

| Platform | Main purpose | Web management | Virtualization role | Suitable for this lab |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Proxmox VE | Virtualization management | Yes | Primary platform | Strong candidate |
| Ubuntu Server | General Linux server | Not included by default | Can host virtual machines using additional software | Strong candidate |
| Debian | General Linux server | Not included by default | Can host virtual machines using additional software | Strong candidate |
| Windows Server | Enterprise Windows services | Management tools available | Supports Hyper-V | Optional learning platform |

### Selection Guidance

For a home lab focused on virtualization, multiple operating systems, infrastructure and networking, consider Proxmox VE as the physical server platform.

For a simpler initial server focused on Linux, Docker, databases and application development, consider Ubuntu Server or Debian.

Windows Server can be added later as a virtual machine if the hardware and licensing requirements allow it.

The best option is not automatically the platform with the most features. It is the one that fits the hardware, budget and learning objectives.

