## 5. Hardware Requirements and Compatibility

Before installing an operating system, verify that the physical server is suitable.

### 5.1 CPU

Check:

- Exact CPU model.
- CPU architecture.
- Number of cores and threads.
- Virtualization support.
- IOMMU support if device passthrough is required.
- Compatibility with the selected operating system or hypervisor.

For virtual machines, hardware virtualization support is important.

Intel processors commonly provide Intel VT-x, while AMD processors commonly provide AMD-V.

IOMMU support is useful for certain device passthrough configurations. It is not a requirement for every basic home lab.

### 5.2 RAM

Record:

- Total physical memory.
- Memory generation.
- Memory speed.
- ECC capability, if applicable.
- Maximum supported capacity.
- Available upgrade slots.

The physical host needs memory for its own operation, in addition to memory allocated to virtual machines and other workloads.

Avoid allocating all physical RAM to virtual machines. Leave sufficient memory for the host and its management services.

### 5.3 Storage

Identify:

- Boot drive.
- Virtual machine storage.
- Container storage.
- Database storage.
- Backup destination.

A simple initial configuration could use one drive for the operating system and another for virtual machine data.

This is only an example. Actual storage design depends on the available drives, reliability requirements and budget.

### 5.4 Network

Confirm:

- Ethernet controller compatibility.
- Driver availability.
- Supported link speed.
- Router and switch compatibility.
- DHCP or static address requirements.

A wired Ethernet connection is generally preferable for a server because it provides a more predictable connection than Wi-Fi.

### 5.5 Compatibility Checklist

- [ ] CPU architecture is supported.
- [ ] CPU virtualization is supported.
- [ ] Required virtualization features are available in firmware.
- [ ] RAM capacity is sufficient.
- [ ] Storage devices are detected.
- [ ] Network interfaces are supported.
- [ ] The system can boot from the intended installation media.
- [ ] The motherboard firmware is suitable.
- [ ] Cooling is adequate.
- [ ] Power supply is suitable.

