## 7. Preparing Installation Media

Most server operating systems provide an ISO image.

An ISO image is a file containing the installation environment.

A bootable USB drive allows the physical server to start the installation environment.

### General Preparation Process

1. Visit the official website of the selected platform.
2. Download the correct installation image.
3. Check the published checksum or signature where available.
4. Use a suitable USB imaging application.
5. Select the downloaded ISO file.
6. Select the correct USB drive.
7. Write the installation image to the USB drive.
8. Safely remove the USB drive.
9. Insert it into the target server.

Examples of commonly used USB imaging applications include:

- Rufus.
- balenaEtcher.
- Ventoy.

Use the official download sources and follow their current instructions.

Do not assume that copying an ISO file onto a USB drive makes it bootable.

